Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?LookupCache:=20pre-commit=20guest-RIP=E2=86=92h?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ost-block=20region=20on=20iOS?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 272MB MEM_RESERVE region for the FEX block-pointer table relies on
auto-commit-on-access-violation through OvercommitTracker. On iOS that
path doesn't take effect cleanly — pages keep faulting after VirtualAlloc(MEM_COMMIT)
returns — so pre-commit the whole region upfront. iOS still demand-faults
physical pages on first touch, so the upfront cost is just VA reservation.

Madeira-commit: 763d4573dd0e0b45fb2ae963000c7c5cd4a22d94
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp
index 0b23030..b9761c8 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp
@@ -38,7 +38,16 @@ LookupCache::LookupCache(FEXCore::Context::ContextImpl* CTX)
   // Allocate a region of memory that we can use to back our block pointers
   // We need one pointer per page of virtual memory
   // At 64GB of virtual memory this will allocate 128MB of virtual memory space
+#ifdef FEX_IOS_HOST
+  /* iOS-Mythic: commit upfront. The auto-commit-on-access-violation path
+   * (OvercommitTracker.HandleAccessViolation) doesn't take effect cleanly
+   * on iOS — pages stay faulting after VirtualAlloc(MEM_COMMIT) returns.
+   * Pre-commit the whole region; physical pages are still demand-faulted
+   * by the kernel. */
+  PagePointer = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(FEXCore::Allocator::VirtualAlloc(TotalCacheSize, false, true));
+#else
   PagePointer = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(FEXCore::Allocator::VirtualAlloc(TotalCacheSize, false, false));
+#endif
   LOGMAN_THROW_A_FMT(PagePointer != -1ULL, "Failed to allocate PagePointer");
 
   // Disable THP on the Lookup cache.
